                          <div class="biGQs _P VImYz AWdfh">
                            <span class="JguWG"
                              >Hello! We returned three days ago; we rented a spectacular house in Nord or Alto Vista,
                              near Arashi Beach. This beach has three differences: one is rocky, the other has waves,
                              and the best part has white sand, like on the rest of the island. We had a great time; we
                              rented a car and toured the island. The experience was very nice; we visited the beaches,
                              which were beautiful, with an incredible water color. The best beach with waves is Boca
                              Catalina, and the widest one with vegetation that provides shade is Eagle Beach. There are
                              places where the width of the beach is 100 meters. There are free public palapas, but they
                              are occupied very early. We went to eat at a place to the south on the day we went to Bebe
                              Beach, by the sea. We ate fresh fish, and it was economical for us. Ten dollars per
                              person. This beach is the best since it is sheltered by a reef and the sea is shallow. It
                              does not have enough shade, and the tents they rent cost 80 dollars. We were surprised
                              that there are no traffic lights, only roundabouts, and people are very respectful while
                              driving. They do not charge for parking anywhere. There are also no lifeguards on the
                              beaches. The water is drinkable and they offer it for free in the restaurants. The
                              temperature is high, close to 30 degrees, and it only drops a little at night. We
                              experienced very dry weather with strong winds all day and night. They say it is usually
                              like this in May. That was the only thing that bothered me; I am an older person. Well, I
                              think I took a screenshot of the island.</span
